          "title": "You'll want to know: सैर",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सैर — sair — \"an outing; a stroll\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "छुट्टी में हम पहाड़ों की सैर पर गए। chuṭṭī meṁ ham pahāṛoṁ kī sair par gae. On holiday we went on a trip to the hills."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सैर (sair) is usually traced to Arabic sayr, \"travel, going about\", through Persian: a trip for pleasure."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
